 arctic areas where fossils  are sparse  figuring out how the Black Death left  its mark on survivors has been difficult  but by studying the ancient DNA of 500  people buried in Europe before during  and after the Black Death researchers  found that survivors had Gene variants  that boosted their immunity to the  fleborne bacterium that causes the  plague one protective variant persists  in some Europeans today but it also puts  these individuals at a higher risk for  developing autoimmune diseases  large-scale clinical trials of two  vaccines against respiratory syncytial  virus or RSV can safely protect the two  groups hardest hit by this common  infection infants and the elderly RSV  vaccine development was derailed for  decades after a trial 50 years ago made  infections worse but the new vaccines  use advanced technology to trigger a far  better antibody response  [Music]  foreign  of the French Antilles researchers  discovered a bacterium up to two  centimeters long five thousand times  longer than a typical microbe unlike  other bacterial cells the margarita  magnifica packages its DNA into sacs  called pepins its unique internal  structure could represent a transitional  form between eukaryotes and prokaryotes  researchers in China showed that a new  strain of perennial rice can survive  year after year and produce crop yields  similar to regular seasonally planted  rice the new strain called perennial  rice 23 is a cross between Asian rice  and a wild rice from Africa perennial  food crops like this could make feeding  the world far less expensive and  labor-intensive  for the first time the U.S passed a law  that could substantially reduce climate  emissions the climate Provisions in the  inflation reduction act will provide 369  billion dollars over 10 years to support  renewable energy and nuclear power  facilitate the shift to electric  vehicles and fund research on Industrial  emissions reductions  while critics say it still isn't enough  to meet globally established targets it  marks the biggest legislative step the  U.S has ever taken to slow global  warming  that wraps up our list of major  advancements for 2022 and our staff is  already looking at the year ahead new  treatments launches and legislation are  just a few of the areas to watch that  will push the boundaries of Science in  2023  [Music]
 

